aarch64 support series for mrustc, against master 1d552cadf1c58bce8b9b431a5714dcea113dde38
(the pinned Source of this recipe).  Eleven fixes, each root-caused on hardware (Axion C4A
lab, then the CS builder) during the arm rustc-1.90 chain campaign, 2026-08-24..27; the arm
chain went R9A_CHAIN_GREEN (all 7 recipe gates) with pin+this on 2026-08-26, and the amd64
revalidation build then caught fix 5's first draft (see below) — the series is measured on
BOTH arches.

Shared-code fixes (affect BOTH arches — the reason this patch applies unconditionally):
  1. static_borrow_constants: GLOBAL fixpoint across modules with interleaved insert +
     insert-ungenerated, replacing the uncaught `Defer` escape (aarch64 libcore trigger,
     shared machinery).
  2. ArraySized visitor override chains to the default visitor (element exprs of [expr; N]
     were never visited -> undetected generics).
  3. Per-slot idempotence guards for double-visited nodes (incl. post-rebind TypeData insert).
  4. res_type sweep in the extract visitor.
  5. f128 alignment tracks u128's EFFECTIVE alignment (the emitted C f128 wraps uint128_t):
     16 with native __int128 (aarch64 — f64's 8 failed TUP_2(f128,f32) 24-vs-32), 8 when
     i128 is EMULATED (x86_64 — an unconditional 16 failed TUP_2(f128,i32) 32-vs-24 on the
     first amd64 build; caught by the emitted sizeof_asserts both times).
  6. Unpacked repr(simd): pow2-size alignment capped at 16, guarded on max_alignment==0
     (core_simd's Simd is repr(simd,packed) and must keep element alignment).
 10. Native-__int128 ctpop: __builtin_popcountll takes a 64-bit argument, so the non-emulated
     emission silently truncated a native u128/i128 to its low half (ctpop(u128::MAX) == 64,
     surfacing as impossible E0080s in downstream const-eval).  Count both halves.  x86_64
     never executed this path (emulated_i128=true -> the correct popcount128 helper).

aarch64-only fixes:
  7. asm!: aarch64 register classes (reg -> "r", vreg -> "w") in expand/asm.cpp, hir/asm.hpp,
     trans/codegen_c.cpp.
  8. asm! template modifiers {N:w}/{N:x} -> GCC %wN/%xN (same letters, pass through).
  9. llvm.aarch64.{isb,dmb,dsb} intrinsics -> real __asm__ __volatile__ barrier instructions
     (strongest "sy" variant) instead of no-ops.

(Numbering note: 11 = the emulated-i128 revision of 5, folded into 5's entry above.)

Cross-cutting lesson encoded twice (5 and 10): mrustc's 128-bit story FORKS on
m_backend_c.m_emulated_i128, and x86_64-linux-gnu is EMULATED while aarch64-linux-gnu is
NATIVE — any layout or intrinsic touching 128-bit types must be written against BOTH modes.

Upstream candidature: to be assessed against lb#470-style originality review before any
public claim; fixes 1-6 and 10 are believed novel, 7-9 partially overlap upstream branches.
